  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "normal_rstan",
      "note": "chain_value assertions removed after CI run 28657005803 (Ubuntu glibc + Windows MSVC both tripped 3 of these 3 platforms apart) -- HMC's default gradient is bound-aware finite differences, so an ~1-ULP libm difference (glibc/MSVC vs Apple libsystem_m) in the Normal log-likelihood divides by h~1e-5, amplifying to ~1e-11 relative gradient noise that leapfrog integrates through the MAP/DE-initialized path, occasionally flipping an early accept/reject decision. macOS (the curation platform) and the dotnet oracle gate still reproduce these values against the real C# library -- only the cross-platform digest is dropped, per the divergence playbook (never widen a tolerance to paper over a stream divergence). chain_fitness at the same indices passed on every platform in that run and is left untouched.",
      "construct": {
        "model": {
          "name": "uniform_constraints",
          "family": "Normal",
          "dataset": "tippecanoe"
        },
        "settings": {
          "step_size": 2.5,
          "steps": 10
        }
      },
